+## SECTION VIII — TEMPORAL BLENDING ENGINE DEFINITIONS (Temporal Blending)
+
+### PAT-032 · Temporal Blending Engine (TBE)
+**Type**: Orchestration Architecture
+**Definition**: A multi-agent architecture designed to resolve Chronotopological Drift when fusing temporally divergent conceptual spaces under the governance of the Verifiable Cognition Stack (VCS).
+
+### PAT-033 · Causal Path Integrity (CPI)
+**Type**: Metric / Governance Constraint
+**Definition**: A mathematically formal constraint enforced by the System Assurance Agent, quantifying the degree of logical adherence to the laws of cause-and-effect over a discrete trace of states generated by an LLM. Requires threshold CPI >= 0.95.
+
+### PAT-034 · Chronotopological Drift
+**Type**: Phenomenon / Pathological Decay
+**Definition**: Sudden, discontinuous jumps in the latent trajectory of generated semantic flows across disjoint semantic territories, violating temporal causal logic. Prevented via enforcing Epistemic Rheology bounds.
+
+### PAT-035 · System Assurance Agent (SAA)
+**Type**: Agent
+**Definition**: The entity responsible for verifying the Causal Path Integrity (CPI) across generated discrete state transitions and enforcing the >0.95 threshold, intercepting violations and triggering Reflexive Repair.
+
+### PAT-036 · Epistemic Rheology
+**Type**: Mathematical Concept
+**Definition**: The continuous flow and deformation of semantic concepts under temporal and logical constraints. Governed by a semantic viscosity parameter ($\mu$) to limit spatial jumps in generated trajectories.
+
+### PAT-037 · Cost of Coherence Overhead (CCH)
+**Type**: Metric
+**Definition**: The computational resources and tokens expended to maintain semantic rigor and verify constraints via deep symbolic modeling. Scales with Verification Depth x Tokens.
+
+### PAT-038 · Cost of Structural Discovery (CSD)
+**Type**: Metric
+**Definition**: The computational budget allocated to explore low-probability regions of the latent space (Intentional Drift) to generate novelty. Scales with Temperature (T) x Variance.
+
